## Start here

- The terminal below runs Claude Code: `claude --continue` picks this folder's conversation up; `/clear` starts afresh.
- Your repositories are in `{{ code_root }}`: `cd {{ code_root }}/<repo>`.
- `gh pr create` and `gh pr checks` work once `gh` is signed in.
- Docker runs without sudo: `docker ps`.

## From your machine

| Command | Does |
|---|---|
| `make code VM_NAME={{ name }}` | open this window again |
| `make claude-login VM_NAME={{ name }}` | sign Claude Code in |
{% if github_auth | default(true) | bool %}
| `make github-login VM_NAME={{ name }}` | sign `gh` in, then clone the private repositories |
{% endif %}
{% if tailscale_enabled | default(true) | bool %}
| `make tailscale-login VM_NAME={{ name }}` | sign it in to Tailscale |
{% endif %}
| `make configure VM_NAME={{ name }}` | run the configuration again; `TAGS=<role>` for one part of it |
| `make list` · `make logs` | the fleet · the run logs |
| `make destroy VM_NAME={{ name }}` | sign it out of everything, then delete it |

## When something is off

- **No Claude terminal, and no notes?** Trust the window (the Restricted Mode banner, Manage, Trust), then allow automatic tasks ("Tasks: Manage Automatic Tasks"), or run "Tasks: Run Task", Claude.
- **Signed in is stale?** "Tasks: Run Task", **Session notes** refreshes it.
- **VS Code asked whether to open this file?** In a one-project window it lies outside the window's folder. Open is remembered for that window; trusting the window of `make code VM_NAME={{ name }}` once avoids the question in every project's.
- **"REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION HAS CHANGED"** after a rebuild: `ssh-keygen -R {{ vm.address }}` on your machine.
{% if claude_code_remote_control | default(true) | bool %}
- **Not in the Claude apps?** `systemctl status {{ code_remote_control_unit }}` here, then `make configure VM_NAME={{ name }} TAGS=claude_code` on your machine.
{% endif %}
- **Private repositories missing?** `make configure VM_NAME={{ name }} TAGS=github_projects` on your machine.

## About this file

Written by `make code` and `make deploy` into `{{ code_notes_dir }}`; its "Signed in" section is rewritten by the window's **Session notes** task each time the window opens. Delete it any time; `vscode_session_notes: false` in your inventory stops it.
